 of these you assume one of them's going  to so who's it going to be and that kind  of pulls you through the movie so I I  felt like that was one of the clever  ideas from the get-go that I love that  you can just get launched into this  chase that goes on and on and it's way  more intimate because it's such a small  cast because there aren't so many people  and I feel like there usually is a huge  there's a large amount of people in a  slasher film and this is totally  different and there's a lot of trust  between them but the adrenaline that you  feel while you're filming it like you're  in it you're there it's happening to you  um yeah I would also say like I feel  like matching the energy of your other  um cast members and the the  circumstances that you're given is  really important in terms of like going  there it's and also like I feel like we  were also very lucky in the sense that  there are very real circumstances that  we were quite literally just come out of  and so there was a lot of  unpacking that we had to do just in  general with the movie that we were able  to do again like on screen so I would  say just for any actor take care of  yourself when you're not there like  really like Let Yourself Go and relax  but when you're there like that that is  where your heart and focus should be and  honestly just have fun doing a slasher  is the best for the funnest thing ever  it's the best form of therapy  I have to let you guys go and it's  breaking my heart right now but you know  what I'm doing now I need to ask you a  scream question I feel like I could have  like a mile long list and keep you here  all day but one of the ones that I  really want to know your take on is  whenever it comes to like the most  iconic slasher franchises I feel like  people often roll their eyes when they  continue on and on and on however  because scream evolves as the genre in  general evolves it makes me think that  it could go on and on forever is that  how you feel about 